Z||000000||Jake_Dragon||08-30-2001||06:47 PM||||Ok here is my sad saga.<BR>When I first purchased my car I had a terrible oil leak.   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smiley_watchout.gif">  This is on an 85 SC 2.5L. <BR>I thought it was due to a leaking seal. Upon further investigation I found my leak at the oil pressure sensor was my problem. To make matters worse I used the 30-weight oil and ran out 3 quarts before I could get it fixed. Ok problem solved?   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smiley_brow.gif">  Well on the way home today I loose all oil pressure and see smoke coming from my vents,   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smiley_wtf.gif">  I shut it down and coast into the next available driveway.   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/eek.gif"> (Glad it wasn’t paved.) Open the hood and the back of my car is covered in oil. Having just change my filter I thought I may have not tightened it, Nope tight as can be. I look at the oil pressure sensor and think could it be that? I dumped 2 quarts of oil in it and got it the 2 blocks home. Now my question is could this be due to the 20w 50 I am using? Was it just too much oil pressure and caused it to blow? My pressure has been right at 40 when idling and around 62 when driving.  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smiley_dizzy.gif">  <P>------------------<BR><A HREF="http://web.tampabay.rr.com/jakedragon" TARGET=_blank>        <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/logo.gif">        </A><p>[This message has been edited by Jake_Dragon (edited 08-30-2001).]||||reg||1
Z||000001||Jake_Dragon||08-30-2001||06:49 PM||||.<p>[This message has been edited by Jake_Dragon (edited 08-30-2001).]||||reg||1
Z||000002||starfighter007@msn.com||08-30-2001||06:58 PM||||so watcha sayen the oil leaked from the sender? If so its probobaly bad sender .I dont think the oil weight has much to do with it .and you may want too check P.C.V. those are my thoughts  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smiley_dizzy.gif">||||reg||1
